{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per","id":781307,"title":"How many Dragonblooded per","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-06T13:51:24-08:00","id":781307,"title":"How many Dragonblooded per","content":"How many Dragonblooded per: <br /> - Great House<br /> - great house family branch<br /> - lesser house of the realm<br /> - non-realm houses (Lookshy or otherwise) <br /> - other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:38:25-08:00","id":781345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great House</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably around 800-1000. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">great house family branch</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe a couple hundred at the highest. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">lesser house of the realm</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">non-realm houses</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say less than fifty for everybody but Lookshy, who are probably more like a Great House branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:57:17-08:00","id":781358,"title":"","content":"How many mortals in said houses above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:01:13-08:00","id":781362,"title":"","content":"The only hard numbers we ever had ahve been:<br /> <br /> 10,000ish in the Realm, with a population of 100 million mortals on the Isle. This includes Dynasts and Lost Eggs, likely cadet and minor houses too.<br /> <br /> 3,000ish in Lookshy, with a total of about 300,000ish people total as resident.<br /> <br /> Probably a few thousand more beyond that who never have been given any numbers save vague &quot;5-10 thousand mortals per DB&quot;, which honestly resulted in fairly inflated numbers at times.<br /> <br /> In 3e any of this is subject to change. Anything else is kind of pulling from ass as reasonable.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:38:52-08:00","id":781417,"title":"","content":"3,000 DBs in Lookshy? One city state = 3/10 of the entire realm dbs, that seems really high. Additionally 1/10000 would mean that the eastern direction would likely have as many DBs as the blessed isle (if not even closely as cohesively bonded). <br /> I always thought the blessed idle had at least 60-70% of the DBs in Creation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:52:40-08:00","id":781427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781417#post781417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3,000 DBs in Lookshy? One city state = 3/10 of the entire realm dbs, that seems really high. Additionally 1/10000 would mean that the eastern direction would likely have as many DBs as the blessed isle (if not even closely as cohesively bonded).<br /> I always thought the blessed idle had at least 60-70% of the DBs in Creation</div> </div> </div> </div>Lookshy is stated as having 1:100 ratio of DBs to mortals. It has a trade-off in that Lookshyan breeding tneds to be pretty poor compared to the Realm, whatever that translates to later. <br /> <br /> The 1:10,000 was from the 1e Storyteller's Companion and for the Blessed Isle originally. In 2e this was extended to everwyhere at 1:5,000-10,000, but as you note, that's a shitload of Dragon-Blooded and probably is overly generous a number. I would sooner just get rid of that as a global statistic and have it so that there's probably a couple thousand other Dragon-Blooded per direction at best, often in small groups or running their own kingdoms, like Prasad.<br /> <br /> And stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:54:53-08:00","id":781430,"title":"","content":"Lookshy has higher numbers than other places specifically because they're shooting for high numbers. The Realm could also hypothetically churn out more DBs if they so desired, but &quot;more DBs = more better&quot; is not the end-all be-all winning strategy that folks seem to think it is, and the Empress was smart enough to realize this.<br /> <br /> (That said, I think the numbers listed earlier are off with regard to Outcaste non-Lookshy DBs.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sidereal'd by a cat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-06-2015, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:57:55-08:00","id":781434,"title":"","content":"Hmm, with the high amount of terrestrials having been around, and the flattening of power levels, does this mean the usurpation may have had bigger wars with Solar DB's heading their armies vs the usurpers DB armies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:59:42-08:00","id":781435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781434#post781434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Solar DB's...</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite its presence in the fiction anthology, you can't be a Solar and a Dragon-Blooded at the same time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:02:48-08:00","id":781438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781435#post781435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite its presence in the fiction anthology, you can't be a Solar and a Dragon-Blooded at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry that should have read. Solar's DBs. As in DB households loyal to the Solars. Raemus got me thinking about if there would have been such a thing, and if so the numbers of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:07:06-08:00","id":781439,"title":"","content":"One thing to note is while Dragon-Blooded are more numerous than other Exalts, the stuff like there being a million Dragon-Blooded in the First Age might be something we won't see revisited. That had a consequence of making DBs seem expendable if you could just breed them to such numbers. I wouldn't be surprised if there always wasn't myriads of Dragon-Blooded for most of history, just concentrated in different amounts around the world.<br /> <br /> That also said, my guess is the Great Uprising probably did have some brother-against-brother shit going down. That of course doesn't change the present situation of things much since we know who won.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:39:47-08:00","id":781456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781439#post781439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That had a consequence of making DBs seem expendable if you could just breed them to such numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that kind of part of the point of them? That they can make good their losses via breeding, which other Exalt types cannot do? I swear to god I recall seeing almost that exact phrase written down somewhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:40:01-08:00","id":781457,"title":"","content":"In addition to what's already been mentioned with Dragon-Blooded numbers Third Edition has introduced the Empire of Prasad if any of the new locations are going to challenge existing demographics its there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:40:56-08:00","id":781459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781438#post781438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry that should have read. Solar's DBs. As in DB households loyal to the Solars. Raemus got me thinking about if there would have been such a thing, and if so the numbers of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would have called them Loyalist DBs versus Usurper DBs, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:56:29-08:00","id":781471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781456#post781456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that kind of part of the point of them? That they can make good their losses via breeding, which other Exalt types cannot do? I swear to god I recall seeing almost that exact phrase written down somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a &quot;Can make up losses via breeding&quot; and &quot;They're nameless cannon fodder&quot;. There's actually a fine line to cross in that and I think while tens of thousands is sitll a lot, there felt like this numbers creep with them over time as there seemed more and more a theme of them as &quot;fodder&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:02:06-08:00","id":781475,"title":"","content":"What's Prasad?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781439#post781439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to note is while Dragon-Blooded are more numerous than other Exalts, the stuff like there being a million Dragon-Blooded in the First Age might be something we won't see revisited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the First Age was supposed to have around 10 billion mortals, so 1 million DBs doesn't seem inflated to me.<br /> <br /> Also I thought the Realm had a little over half of the DBs in Creation, including lost eggs and cadet houses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:22:35-08:00","id":781485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781475#post781475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's Prasad?</div> </div> </div> </div>The city of Kamthahar in the Southeast is the capital of the empire of Prasad, the Realm's most distant (and heretical) satrapy. The Dragon-Blooded here follow an offshoot of the Immaculate Philosophy called the Pure Way, and are worshiped as gods by their people. They allow actual gods and such to be worshiped as long as the Dragon-Blooded are given the highest prominence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T20:16:13-08:00","id":781503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781471#post781471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cannon fodder<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator said it better than me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/580376-terrestrial-exalted-limited-numbers?p=582926#post582926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the term &quot;cannon fodder&quot; often gets misused by people who aren't really aware of a prior tactical reality in which certain troops getting indiscriminately cut down by weapons fire was kind of an inescapable reality, and even then it refers mostly to an idea of either putting your least valuable troops at the front of the formation so that the ones killed in the opening volleys are a minimal loss, or the ineptitude of commanders advancing troops in maneuvers in which they'll be unnecessarily exposed to volleys for minimal gain.<br /> <br /> It does <i>not</i> refer to the basic, unfortunate reality that in heavy fighting, you are going to get a fair amount of troops get torn apart indiscriminately or that part of commanding a battle includes a willingness to order troops to their deaths.<br /> <br /> Which are things I <i>would</i> expect to be part of the assumptions and experience of the Dragon Blooded. Not always quite as enthusiastic as the aforementioned War Boys leaping into a literally explosive fray, but I would say that qualities including their numbers and means of replacement mean that in military matters, there can be an awareness and acceptance of the idea that being on the front lines means that somebody is sure to die, or that there are going to be operations in which one is asked to risk or give their life. I mean, there are surely any Exalted who are going to be capable of such sentiments, some Solar Exalt who would opt to stay in a mortally dangerous situation so that others might escape despite some quasi-rationalists insistence that their life is surely of greater value than that of any number of mortals and they should prioritize their own safety and future, but... again, it's a matter of assessing culture and attitude, even practical results.<br /> <br /> To be Terrestrial Exalted is not to be insignificant or interchangeable, but they can be many in a way that means the world doesn't stop turning and the fight doesn't stop raging if some should fall. Not because they were worthless, but because they know that there's a sibling or a child or a comrade waiting at their back to step into their place and continue forward. A sense of expandability not because some distant commander saw you only as a pawn to be moved or sacrificed at their will, but because you know your death won't be the end of things, and can even create openings to achieve things.<br /> <br /> You know, little things that place the Dragon Blooded in a context of agency and humanity and basic dignity, rather than a product in some manse fetishism.<br /> <br /> Also things that lend insight into the actual priority behind Dragon Blooded families; you're not making a horde, you're binding together partners and ensuring a line of succession.<br /> <br /> Referring to the idea of people as cannon fodder with sincerity and enthusiasm, well... if you've ever read any poetry by a World War I veteran in which the writer elaborates on their mildly exaggerated view of their armchair generals, you might have some indications as to their character.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:07:02-08:00","id":781531,"title":"","content":"This I would argue is an example of the term probably being less &quot;misused&quot; and more changed in meaning since its initial use in regular parlance. Like well, dozens of other random words. But I would think the term as used today is because such a state is considered unfortunate and has been since about World War II and no later than I would think the US-Vietnam War.<br /> <br /> So while it is a bit of interesting pedantry in the historic ontology of a term, terms change. See my general snarkiness at times with dinosaurs, for instance. And in the context of what I meant to highlight, too inflated of numbers for Terrestrial Exalted result in a perception of them being expendable. I think an idea that the number today, as the recovered population post-Contagion Era, shows more to how potential badass it was in the past. Rather than the situation I got out of <b>Dreams of the First Age</b>, which left me feeling that Dragon-Blooded needed to apparently be orders of magnitude greater in population to even have a chance of mattering for Creation's &quot;real&quot; potential.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T22:38:34-08:00","id":781568,"title":"","content":"The problem with the 10,000 Terrestrials in the Realm number is that the census that gave us that number took place a few years before the defeat of the Tepet legions in the North and before the fall of Thorns that was backed by the Realm with Terrestrials when Mask of Winters attacked.<br /> <br /> All in all if you consider the numbers of Terrestrials that got &quot;worfed&quot; in each supplement or random recent conflict recaps, the Realm Terrestrial population is probably around 9,000 currently. Divide that by the number of great houses, then shuffle around the numbers to reflect the sizes of each given great house (V'Neef has like less than a dozen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T01:16:16-08:00","id":781603,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the number isn't from a census, it's mostly propaganda. It's just an idea: &quot;10,000 Dragons conquer the world!&quot; It's about 10,000, or over 10,000. So I wouldn't get too obsessed with the exact number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T03:36:56-08:00","id":781633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781434#post781434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, with the high amount of terrestrials having been around, and the flattening of power levels, does this mean the usurpation may have had bigger wars with Solar DB's heading their armies vs the usurpers DB armies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really think of that as something to do with the power curve, not least because the Usurpation can't really be represented mechanically. I mean, how would the fight between Desus' statblock in Lords of Creation handle a couple of hundred Terrestrials attacking him at once? N/A.<br /> <br /> I personally picture the Usurpation as having gotten through its initial stage dramatically quickly; something like half of the Solars who actually attended the feast (who were themselves not the full number of Solars, somewhere between half and two-thirds) being killed in the first couple of days, several dozen also being assassinated in short order (some more loudly than others) in their own holdings shortly thereafter, then several weeks of terrible purges and occasional carpet bombing that leave only about twenty surviving. The the Jade Prison gets sealed.<br /> <br /> The Exalted who reincarnated throughout the Second Age manage to adopt strategies that take a few years of warfare that devastates much of Creation (if you're not directly fighting in it, you're sure as hell funding it). Some of these Solars might have a few die-hard Terrestrials still alongside them, but I imagine that most Dragon Blooded gamble on their fellows when the first word came down the pipeline, and a lot of the ones who were most dedicated were targets for initial purges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781439#post781439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the stuff like there being a million Dragon-Blooded in the First Age might be something we won't see revisited. That had a consequence of making DBs seem expendable if you could just breed them to such numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the idea that even in the realms of retrospect and speculation, such a number probably isn't the best idea, but mostly for concerns of it being arbitrarily high and possibly creating a bit of dissonance about what they were actually doing.<br /> <br /> Otherwise... what exactly would they be expended on?<br /> <br /> And how many expendable Dragon Blooded are we talking about here? A few dozen? A few hundred? Under what circumstances? From what I can gather and logically extrapolate, having a million rare people of singular expertise wouldn't keep the death of a few hundred of them all at once in a single theater from being a disaster.<br /> <br /> It's like... you think you have large stockpiles of food until you go a couple of days without food shipments, and then you realise just how frequently the community needs to restock.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781471#post781471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a fine line to cross in that and I think while tens of thousands is sitll a lot, there felt like this numbers creep with them over time as there seemed more and more a theme of them as &quot;fodder&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those numbers were more a matter of the scale they were ascribing to that vision of the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T03:37:26-08:00","id":781634,"title":"","content":"I'm annoyed; I don't think my quote against ridiculous arguments that Dragon Blooded should optimally be treated as Zergs is actually relevant to this context, and I don't want to have an argument about my statement aboiut the term. <br /> <br /> I duisaEDFGFTRERE with NBlaqque's assessmnehnhntt. Words dp change, but theycam still be used in ignorance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T04:38:57-08:00","id":781651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781634#post781634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm annoyed; I don't think my quote against ridiculous arguments that Dragon Blooded should optimally be treated as Zergs is actually relevant to this context, and I don't want to have an argument about my statement aboiut the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T06:22:01-08:00","id":781678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781475#post781475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's Prasad?<br /> I think the First Age was supposed to have around 10 billion mortals, so 1 million DBs doesn't seem inflated to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statistically the numbers are reasonable, the number of Dragon-Blooded is a lot less than the number of millionaires in the real world and you could fit all of them into a reasonable sized city. But some people see &quot;one million&quot; and their sense of scale shuts down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T07:03:04-08:00","id":781686,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the number of them might have come across worse when presented in terms of them being already organised into quasi-Great Houses. There were, what, five hundred of those? So you end up with family units consisting of about two thousand Exalted each?<br /> <br /> I dispute the point of them being nameless and indiscriminate (or at least of its significance, since that's really going to be the case anyway), but it feels a bit... heavy.<br /> <br /> At the same time... I think the presentation of a large number might create that sense of &quot;Dragon Blooded are doing things everywhere&quot;, which rather than coming across as expendable makes them feel far too necessary and ubiquitous, at the same time as it doesn't actually hold up when the ratios are considered.<br /> <br /> These are all the kinds of things that make me view the Dragon Blooded of the First Age as having been more about expanding laterally; that it was better to be an individual and went off to form families with &quot;locally&quot; prominent figures to spread out dynasties that could produce one or two Exalted per generation to carry out the presence of the Realm, or for the powerful family lines to be based on ownership of significant rights and properties while also producing favoured children who could go off and join the central or patrolling institutions of the Realm, or attach themselves to the projects of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> To the extent that such a thing is significant in games, I could put hints of it into First Age stories for Exalted characters to come across for the sake of contrasting eras or having insight into alternative social models.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T08:46:03-08:00","id":781708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781678#post781678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Statistically the numbers are reasonable, the number of Dragon-Blooded is a lot less than the number of millionaires in the real world and you could fit all of them into a reasonable sized city. But some people see &quot;one million&quot; and their sense of scale shuts down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is exactly the case. The word &quot;million&quot; while not big in teh context of 10 billion, is so huge in context of tens of thousands that it feels like some threshold is crossed to me.<br /> <br /> I would agree with Levi it might just be issues of scale with the presentation of the First Age, which were kind of weirdly all over the place and inconsistent in both how some areas are presented as big and diverse (West, East) and others the author felt it was needed to talk about every single solitary dominion on the map in some detail (North, Center). So at times you had things which looked like it fit the numbers nad you had others which didn't seem to do a lot to use the numbers save for fantasy/sci-fi inflationary purposes.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T09:32:20-08:00","id":781728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781603#post781603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the number isn't from a census, it's mostly propaganda. It's just an idea: &quot;10,000 Dragons conquer the world!&quot; It's about 10,000, or over 10,000. So I wouldn't get too obsessed with the exact number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it is.<br /> <br /> <b><u>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded \u2013 page 226 </u></b><br /> \u201cThe 761 Realm census placed the number of Dynastic Dragon-Blooded in the Realm (included lost eggs adopted to Great Houses) near 10,000. This might be as many as half the entire world\u2019s population of Terrestrial Exalted, and the world knows that it\u2019s there.\u201d<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T10:53:13-08:00","id":781753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per#post781307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Dragonblooded per:<br /> - other</div> </div> </div> </div>The Forest Witches have about 80 living Dragon-Blooded and this makes them a power capable of independence with Halta and Linowan as neighbors. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:49:52-08:00","id":781941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781728#post781728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it is.<br /> <br /> <b><u>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded \u2013 page 226 </u></b><br /> \u201cThe 761 Realm census placed the number of Dynastic Dragon-Blooded in the Realm (included lost eggs adopted to Great Houses) near 10,000. This might be as many as half the entire world\u2019s population of Terrestrial Exalted, and the world knows that it\u2019s there.\u201d<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T19:33:42-08:00","id":782030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=781531#post781531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an idea that the number today, as the recovered population post-Contagion Era, shows more to how potential badass it was in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's reasonable to depict Creation as having recovered, even in human population, from the Contagion. 90% of all life died, followed by the majority of the plague survivors (due to Fair Folk.) That's ~95-99% of all animals, plants, elementals, gods, and humans. That must have caused famine, mass extinction, soil infertility, massive erosion, huge wildfires as the dead stuff dries up and burns, follow-up (mundane) disease problems as the dead bodies rot and foul the water, etc. 90% of all individual living creatures is the estimated death-toll for the mass extinction that ended the Cretaceous and killed the dinosaurs. After things like that, the real world doesn't recover (in biodiversity and ecosystem health) for <i><b>millions</b></i> of years.<br /> <br /> Now you have people who've been bombed back into the stone age (or at best the bronze age) and quite literally abandoned by Heaven, the Terrestrial gods are all fucked up, there are mutants and Fair Folk still running around killing people. The landscape is utterly denuded, much of it uninhabitable. Even after weeds and grass start to grow again (and it won't be like after a wildfire, because the Contagion would have killed off the seeds in the soil as well. It would be more like primary succession after a volcano covers everything in lava), I think it would take at least a few centuries just for most of the landscape to actually be able to support human life. The Realm got a head start in that maybe, but most of Creation realistically could not have had conditions in which human populations <b><i>could</i></b> grow for maybe the first half of the Age of Sorrows. After that people can start to spread out into the landscape and with the empty space, there will be some population growth. But it would be the population growth of a stone age or bronze age world that is still hugely lethal, not the exponential population increase of our modern industrial world. So maybe over the entire Age of Sorrows, the overall human population could have doubled just <i><b>once</b></i>.<br /> <br /> I doubt it's depicted this way in the books, but this is what I would consider believable, with most of the kingdoms and empires in the outer Directions being only a couple centuries old, and with soil fertility and living conditions still mostly very poor. 750 years is not enough for a species to recover from an apocalypse that extreme, especially not when most gods and Exalted refuse to actually do anything to rebuild.<br /> <br /> Maybe in the Blessed Isle with whatever it is they do force gods to cooperate and make the soil fertile and the weather not suck, the human population could have tripled or even quadrupled, if I'm generous. But even if the Realm was dedicated to breeding above all else, without a religion that encourages 1/3 of the Exalted to be celibate, they just couldn't have recovered the Dragon-Blooded host to their pre-Contagion population. It just isn't plausible to me at all.<br /> <br /> Which kind of goes with something I've thought about before, which is that the Contagion as depicted (at least in 1E-2E) is not only far in excess of what's necessary to set up a post-apocalypse setting. It actually makes the present-day setting's relative recovery implausible, and also sets up every NPC who supports the current status quo to be dumber than rocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-07-2015, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T19:57:03-08:00","id":782042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=782030#post782030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...most gods and Exalted refuse to actually do anything to rebuild.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, see, there's your trouble. First step, disabuse yourself of this notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T20:08:54-08:00","id":782047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=782030#post782030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's reasonable to depict Creation as having recovered, even in human population, from the Contagion. 90% of all life died, followed by the majority of the plague survivors (due to Fair Folk.) That's ~95-99% of all animals, plants, elementals, gods, and humans. That must have caused famine, mass extinction, soil infertility, massive erosion, huge wildfires as the dead stuff dries up and burns, follow-up (mundane) disease problems as the dead bodies rot and foul the water, etc. 90% of all individual living creatures is the estimated death-toll for the mass extinction that ended the Cretaceous and killed the dinosaurs. After things like that, the real world doesn't recover (in biodiversity and ecosystem health) for <i><b>millions</b></i> of years.<br /> <br /> Now you have people who've been bombed back into the stone age (or at best the bronze age) and quite literally abandoned by Heaven, the Terrestrial gods are all fucked up, there are mutants and Fair Folk still running around killing people. The landscape is utterly denuded, much of it uninhabitable. Even after weeds and grass start to grow again (and it won't be like after a wildfire, because the Contagion would have killed off the seeds in the soil as well. It would be more like primary succession after a volcano covers everything in lava), I think it would take at least a few centuries just for most of the landscape to actually be able to support human life. The Realm got a head start in that maybe, but most of Creation realistically could not have had conditions in which human populations <b><i>could</i></b> grow for maybe the first half of the Age of Sorrows. After that people can start to spread out into the landscape and with the empty space, there will be some population growth. But it would be the population growth of a stone age or bronze age world that is still hugely lethal, not the exponential population increase of our modern industrial world. So maybe over the entire Age of Sorrows, the overall human population could have doubled just <i><b>once</b></i>.<br /> <br /> I doubt it's depicted this way in the books, but this is what I would consider believable, with most of the kingdoms and empires in the outer Directions being only a couple centuries old, and with soil fertility and living conditions still mostly very poor. 750 years is not enough for a species to recover from an apocalypse that extreme, especially not when most gods and Exalted refuse to actually do anything to rebuild.<br /> <br /> Maybe in the Blessed Isle with whatever it is they do force gods to cooperate and make the soil fertile and the weather not suck, the human population could have tripled or even quadrupled, if I'm generous. But even if the Realm was dedicated to breeding above all else, without a religion that encourages 1/3 of the Exalted to be celibate, they just couldn't have recovered the Dragon-Blooded host to their pre-Contagion population. It just isn't plausible to me at all.<br /> <br /> Which kind of goes with something I've thought about before, which is that the Contagion as depicted (at least in 1E-2E) is not only far in excess of what's necessary to set up a post-apocalypse setting. It actually makes the present-day setting's relative recovery implausible, and also sets up every NPC who supports the current status quo to be dumber than rocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note I mean the Dragon-Blooded population. My understanding is that the Exalted are still pretty resiliant to the Contagion (I don't assume the 1e or 2e rules for it). This means that the Dragon-Blooded likely lost more numbers in the Balorian Crusade and I'm skeptical they had more individuals in the Shogunate than they do now after a few years of population growth.<br /> <br /> Anything value-based on attempts to recover Creation is another factor and for another thread, but I want to just clarify that i meant Dragon-Blooded, not really anything else.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T20:34:07-08:00","id":782053,"title":"","content":"Even if you're going with an idea that Exalted were resistant to it (which isn't my understanding) for a population to grow they still need food, water, inhabitable land, shelter, infrastructure, etc. Even medicine, since the children are ordinary mortals until they exalt at whatever age, which means infant mortality is exactly as lethal as for any other humans, dependant on whatever public hygiene and medical care is available. And the Realm culture doesn't even encourage maximum-possible DB population growth.<br /> <br /> Also I forgot to mention that the Contagion would also have killed 95-99% of the stored seeds farmers had prepared for the next planting, and with famine looming people would tend to eat what was left, which may mean that most people lost the ability to farm altogether, and thus the landscape recovered slower than it could have with human help. Agriculture would then have to have spread slowly from surviving pockets, one crop from here and one from there... in other words I think that realistically we're talking &quot;bombed back into the paleolithic&quot;, not the bronze age. And when you barely have enough to eat, do you bother teaching your kids how to make bronze or read? No, they're too busy looking for anything to eat. So technological knowledge would have to re-diffuse as well, or be re-invented from scratch.<br /> <br /> One other thing to consider regarding Shogunate numbers it that at that time, the Dragon-Blooded seem to have ruled more of the world than the Scarlet Empire does, and more directly too. That implies to me that their population was not just more spread out over the Directions, but also that it was larger, especially if (as I think) the mortal population was 10 to 100 times higher back then.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, I think my personal headcanon might become that the Contagion only killed humans and at most 70-80% of them, even counting those who died to the Balorian Crusade, which is still a <i><b>huge</b></i> apocalypse, but doesn't break the setting over its knee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-07-2015, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T20:44:38-08:00","id":782057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=782053#post782053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you're going with an idea that Exalted were resistant to it (which isn't my understanding) for a population to grow they still need food, water, inhabitable land, shelter, infrastructure, etc. Even medicine, since the children are ordinary mortals until they exalt at whatever age, which means infant mortality is exactly as lethal as for any other humans, dependant on whatever public hygiene and medical care is available. And the Realm culture doesn't even encourage maximum-possible DB population growth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I feel there's likelihood not as much Terrestrial die-off. The Realm seems to of grown at a decent clip and there didn't see to be a crisis of population for the Dyansty either. This implies to me that it's grownt at fairly natural numbers, but also that there was probably decent amount ot start with. It's especially the case if the Blessed Isle was relatively untouched (which seems to be the case).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=782053#post782053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I forgot to mention that the Contagion would also have killed 95-99% of the stored seeds farmers had prepared for the next planting, and with famine looming people would tend to eat what was left, which may mean that most people lost the ability to farm altogether, and thus the landscape recovered slower than it could have with human help. Agriculture would then have to have spread slowly from surviving pockets, one crop from here and one from there... in other words I think that realistically we're talking &quot;bombed back into the paleolithic&quot;, not the bronze age. And when you barely have enough to eat, do you bother teaching your kids how to make bronze or read? No, they're too busy looking for anything to eat. So technological knowledge would have to re-diffuse as well, or be re-invented from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Population loss seems relatively uneven throughotu Creation in this regard, as a note. And it should be noted that population bounce-back need not follow Earth rates. You ahve an entire Direction based on life as an element and I think that would likely have impacted recovery and such. I think there's also a bit of &quot;Just dont' overthink it&quot; in this area of things, since Exalted is based enough on ancient myth that htat to me helps make things like there even being redwood forests make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=782053#post782053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing to consider regarding Shogunate numbers it that at that time, the Dragon-Blooded seem to have ruled more of the world than the Scarlet Empire does, and more directly too. That implies to me that their population was not just more spread out over the Directions, but also that it was larger, especially if (as I think) the mortal population was 10 to 100 times higher back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know how much more mortals there were. I'm of the opinion the 10 billion number for <b>Dreams of the First Age</b>'s population was an example of making the First Age a near future sci-fi than really anything needed. The Dragon-Blooded population could also be like it is today and rule most of Creation if it were as you note, less centralized and additionally, if it had more a chunk of Terrestrials to it. Since concepts like the Wyld Hunt and such are Shogunate institution now part of Terrestrial culture, I don't see it as unlikely that you could have as many Dragon-Blooded now as there were in the peak of the Shogunate, just rather than just over half claiming loyalty ot the Empress (if that), you could have most claiming some form (if not not actual) loyalty to the Shogun. The infastructure of the time, the unified Host and all that would probably be doable with 20,000 to 30,000 globally compared to the 10,000 regionally of the current Realm. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=782053#post782053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In conclusion, I think my personal headcanon might become that the Contagion only killed humans and at most 70-80% of them, even counting those who died to the Balorian Crusade, which is still a <i><b>huge</b></i> apocalypse, but doesn't break the setting over its knee.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it killing lots of large animal life at hte 90% rate, but other things might have just done better. That or some aspects of the Sword of Creation might have recalibrated stuff. This is a world hwich while working on biology could also have random Aristotlean spontaneous genration, afterall.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T02:05:25-08:00","id":782155,"title":"","content":"Wood Essence creates different premises for recovery of flora and microbes*.<br /> <br /> Large sections of the devastated Creation subsequently disappeared.<br /> <br /> 90% of all life does not need to mean that each individual category of thing was reduced to 10%; it does not need to mean that stored seeds were reduced by that exact figure, assuming they were even targeted at all.<br /> <br /> The Contagion was still threatening to the Exalted. Hell, it's the quintessentially threatening disease to the Exalted. A lot of Terrestrials could have caught it in the early stages just trying to cure it, before it became apparent that that was largely beyond them.<br /> <br /> Spirits are not susceptible to disease.<br /> <br /> The Dragon Blooded were probably greatly reduced in numbers; the Shogunate absolutely had more of them around than the Realm does, the depiction in the Aspect Books make no sense otherwise.<br /> <br /> Depictions which, one should note, still portray the idea of about a hundred Exalted dying in a single battle to be an unprecedented disaster, even while assuming that a hundred Exalted being there in the first place wasn't a big deal in the least.<br /> <br /> * Destroying 90% of most microbes won't stop them anyway. A lot of the good stuff has a doubling time of about twenty minutes; that means that in a single day, one cell becomes hundreds of trillions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:16:07-08:00","id":782286,"title":"","content":"The main place where they really dropped the ball with the notion that the Great Contagion killing 90% of <b>everything</b> is with the really mundane totem animals of the Lunar elders suggesting that in terms of biodiversity nothing of value or interest was lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T10:38:09-08:00","id":782375,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the Contagion spread through the Dragon Lines to hit every single part of Creation, equally, and killed 90% of everything alive including spirits. It's possible the books have been inconsistent. Certainly I consider the picture they paint, overall, inconsistent and nonsensical, hence my complaint.<br /> <br /> I'm more comfortable with spontaneous generation/divine creation restoring extinct species or creating new ones, but it's harder to believe that they could repopulate the entire world so quickly that it now looks as if nothing at all happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T10:54:40-08:00","id":782384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=782375#post782375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's possible the books have been inconsistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh very much so.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Compass Yu-Shan page 15</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Less than two months after the initial outbreak, Ozumi the Brown, God of White-Tailed Wolverines, personally delivered his final report on that creature to the Bureau of Nature, detailing how an entire subspecies had become extinct within just six weeks. Ozumi was lucky\u2014the Celestial Bureaucracy still did not realize the true scope of the disaster, and they simply transferred Ozumi to the Infections Diseases Department of the Bureau of Nature, where more manpower was desperately required.<br /> Soon, the trickle of gods whose portfolios had been annihilated became a flood, and for the first time in its history, the Bureau of Heaven began tracking divine unemployment statistics.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:22:53-08:00","id":782496,"title":"","content":"Do you know one thing that's a big difference between the Great Contagion and real life extinction events? The Great Contagion didn't involve things like changing how the climate or atmosphere worked. I'm pretty sure that most real life extinction events took a long time to recover less because it takes a long time to build numbers or diversity back up again and more because of things like there not being very much sunlight for eons. The Great Contagion merely killed things. It's more like the Black Death than a meteor impact, and the main long term effect of the Black Death was social. I mean, maybe there's a real-life major extinction event that didn't involve a meteor impact or a supervolcano eruption or similar thing that changes the overall temperature and puts large quantities of matter into the atmosphere that I'm missing, and if there is then I would like it pointed out to me, but I think that massive amounts of death that merely comes from disease leaves relatively few scars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T07:43:53-08:00","id":782792,"title":"","content":"On the scale of several millennia, yes. On the scale of a few centuries, it's wildly improbable to me. Not that there wouldn't be forests, wetlands, cities, etc. It is likely the Eastern lands are recovering faster. To one who doesn't know what the world used to be like, Creation's lands may appear lush and healthy and whole, the way that the second-growth brush and monocultures of exotic weeds (and piles of litter) in the park by my home looks normal to somebody who's never seen a healthy climax forest or intact wetland.<br /> <br /> But I can't conceive any way for the population levels of everything, including humans, to bounce back perfectly as if nothing had happened. Rats, dandelions, mosquitoes, bacteria (if they exist), in numbers at least (no clue if &quot;genetic diversity&quot; has any meaning in Creation). Not big creatures. Not the intricate webs of healthy, resilient ecosystems. Not humans or yeddim herds or tyrant lizards. This isn't a setting where the gods can magic entire thriving ecosystems or populous cities into existence from nothing. Nor do I get the impression many would try -- most gods seem to be too selfish to care about the state of Creation, and most Exalted are obsessed only with killing each other and/or getting rich.<br /> <br /> Exponential population growth in slow-breeding species (like humans or mammoths or whales) requires a big change in infant mortality, longevity, and/or age of first child-bearing. Without exponential growth, I don't think slow-breeders can restore a loss of 90% of the population in 7 centuries, especially not while their food source is <i><b>also</b></i> equally depopulated. In fact, if herbivores increase faster than their food source or predators can, they'll denude the landscape all over again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I don't think it's entirely accurate to say that non-living systems in Creation were undamaged. The Fair Folk mangled the dragon-lines, the Terrestrial and Celestial bureaucracies are utterly dysfunctional and not doing their jobs, and there are shadowlands and Wyld zones all over. A state of nonstop warfare has its own devastating effect on the landscape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-09-2015, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T07:57:44-08:00","id":782802,"title":"","content":"I don't think the human population has recovered from the Great Contagion by the Age of Sorrows. There are still plenty of abandoned ruins for PCs to plunder and empty wild place for PCs to hide and practice their abilities without having to worry about someone seeing their Anima.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:38:32-08:00","id":782870,"title":"","content":"Who's to say Ahlat <i>can't</i> create more cattle, say, shaping herds of aurochs out of the dust of the earth and breathing life into them? Or laying a blessing that makes existing cattle more fertile for the next, say, seven generations? Entire fields of frogs or bugs or rats should be even easier given the resonance between gods and plagues.<br /> <br /> And there are entire bureaus of these guys working together (admittedly whilst mired in corruption, but a lot of that corruption is them getting around restrictions or obtaining extra resources) to steer the course of events for the good of Creation (or at least their respective corners of it), even controlling the weather and submitting paperwork detailing algae numbers this season. I don't think the setting looking the way it does is beyond the realm of plausibility the way you seem to think it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-09-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T15:07:40-08:00","id":783073,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if I was going to have a problem with the 90% figure, assuming it included the idea that 90% of humans died, it would be that it was <i>too mild</i>. I mean, how many are we supposed to be starting with? If the population of Creation at the end of the Shogunate was supposed to be about the same as what it was portrayed as in Lands of Creation, then a billion people would have survived the Contagion. If there were significantly fewer, that gives me the issue of how the Shogunate would have been so lethal. And when I say significantly fewer, I mean... see, my image of the aftermath of the Contagion tends to assume that there were fewer people then than there are supposed to be in Creation at present. Sooo... you would have to start off with a smaller population than exists today, because if you killed 90% of the people on actual Earth, you would wind up with 700 million people. Y'know, more than exist in Creation. I guess when one looks at it like that, you could go with the idea that the human population of Creation hasn't really recovered at all. Hell, it seems kind of logical for it to have <i>continued falling</i> over the course of the Age of Sorrows. Which... now that I think about it, I kind of prefer that. So yeah, they're pretty fucked. (The alternative, of course, is to assume that the First Age never had a population anywhere close to our own one, which could work for some people, but just doesn't suit me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T17:32:11-08:00","id":783149,"title":"","content":"Presumably though, the idea is the Great Contagion killed 90% of people, but then with collapsing infrastructure many more died (the population of Britain halved from 400-500, and that was just due to collapsing infrastructure) because things just don't work when 90% of people died. Food production and transport being the most key.<br /> And then an infinite number of soul-eating nightmare monsters invaded.<br /> And then there was an apocalyptic war against them which likely had a lot of collateral damage.<br /> And then the population probably continued to fall due to the lack of infrastructure for a while, before beginning to recover maybe 100 years later or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T20:05:10-08:00","id":783212,"title":"","content":"Yeah, what Wizard said. The death toll was probably around 99%.<br /> <br /> The Contagion alone killed 90% of all life, but then what had survived was mostly wiped out by the Fair Folk, and what survived <b><i>that</i></b> had to contend with famine because everything edible was gone, and the lack of infrastructure and gods and elementals, the dragon lines not flowing right, etc. I think the population could have stopped falling on the Blessed Isle after maybe 100 years, because the Empress and her DB recruits couldn't build an empire until they got that under control, so they were motivated to do something. Blessed Isle populations might have started growing again after 200 or even just 100 years.<br /> <br /> I think populations of humans could have started to increase in the East after maybe 150-300 years... but due in part to migration, not just Wood essence. Human populations might have continued to fall for 200 years or longer in the North and South, and maybe the West too, and perhaps only started to climb 400-500 years after the apocalypse. The Blessed Isle and East might have twice the number of humans today as the number where the population finally bottomed out, or even more than twice. But the other Directions probably haven't doubled their human population even once yet.<br /> <br /> Looking at the numbers that other people have told me are in the books...<br /> 500 million humans today. Half that is 250 million. 100 times that was 25 billion.<br /> From 10 billion in the First Age, 1% would have been 100 million.<br /> <br /> (I'm assuming here that billion means 10<sup>9</sup>, not 10<sup>12</sup>, in the Exalted books since WW/OPP are American. Also because a First Age population of 10<sup>13</sup> would be hard to believe.)<br /> <br /> So if my math is right, then from the Era of Dreams population, the current population is 5%?<br /> <br /> It would make sense that the Shogunate couldn't support a population of 10 billion, though. Aside from the warfare, some/all of the magical infrastructure that supported the high population fell apart or was destroyed. If the population at the end of the Shogunate had been 5 billion,... I am no longer sure what that would mean. I wonder if the figure of 10 billion was decided by multiplying 500 million by 10 (for the Contagion), then by 2 either for the Shogunate + Usurpation, or for the Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> I am, gods help me, going to attempt more math. Actual hypothetical scenarios this time. I'm going to see if I can figure out how 500 million people could have come about.<br /> <br /> <u>Late Shogunate population -&gt; total deathtoll -&gt; population nadir -&gt; population growth -&gt; late Age of Sorrows population.</u><br /> 10 billion -&gt; 99% dead -&gt; 100 million survive -&gt;200% growth -&gt; 200 million. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Wrong result, </b>and improbable starting population.</span><br /> 10 billion -&gt; 95% dead -&gt; 500 million survive -&gt; 0% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b>but lack of growth may be improbable.<br /> 10 billion -&gt; 99% dead -&gt; 100 million survive -&gt; 500% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">but improbable starting number and population growth.</span><br /> 5 billion -&gt; 99% dead -&gt; 50 million survive -&gt; 200% growth -&gt; 100 million. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Wrong result.</b></span><br /> 5 billion -&gt; 99% dead -&gt; 50 million survive -&gt; 1000% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">very improbable population growth.</span><br /> 5 billion -&gt; 90% dead -&gt; 500 million survive -&gt; 0% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b>deathtoll and lack of growth may be improbable.<br /> 3.3 billion -&gt; 90% dead -&gt; 333 million survive -&gt; 150% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result</b><b>, </b>deathtoll and starting population may be improbable.<br /> 2.5 billion -&gt; 90% dead -&gt; 250 million survive -&gt; 200% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b>deathtoll and starting population may be improbable.<br /> 2 billion -&gt; 90% dead -&gt; 200 million survive -&gt; 250% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b>deathtoll and starting population may be improbable.<br /> 4 billion -&gt; 90% dead -&gt; 400 million survive -&gt; 125% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result</b>, maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> 4 billion -&gt; 91.7% dead -&gt; 333 million survive -&gt; 150% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result</b>, maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> 4 billion -&gt; 93.75% dead -&gt; 250 million survive -&gt; 200% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result</b>, maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> 4 billion -&gt; 95% dead -&gt; 200 million survive -&gt; 250% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result</b>, maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> 5 billion -&gt; 95% dead -&gt; 250 million survive -&gt; 200% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result, </b>maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> 7 billion -&gt; 96.4% dead -&gt; 250 million survive -&gt; 200% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result, </b>maybe plausible numbers</span><span style=\"color:#008000\">.</span><br /> 7 billion -&gt; 97% dead -&gt; 210 milion survive -&gt; 238% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result, </b>maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> 25 billion -&gt; 99% dead -&gt; 250 million survive -&gt; 200% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result. </b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Absurd starting population.</span><br /> 16 billion -&gt; 99% dead -&gt; 167 million survive -&gt; 300% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result. </b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Absurd starting population.</span> Growth may be improbable too.<br /> 3.3 billion -&gt; 95% dead -&gt; 167 million survive -&gt; 300% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b>starting population and growth may be improbable.<br /> 5 billion -&gt; 96.7% dead -&gt; 167 million survive -&gt; 300% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result</b><b>. </b>Population growth may be improbable.<br /> 5 billion -&gt; 97% dead -&gt; 150 million survive -&gt; 333% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result.</b> Population growth looks improbable.<br /> 20 billion -&gt; 99% dead -&gt; 200 million survive -&gt; 250% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result. </b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Absurd starting population. </span><br /> 5 billion -&gt; 96% dead -&gt; 200 million survive -&gt; 250% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result, </b>maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> 10 billion -&gt; 98% dead -&gt; 200 million survive -&gt; 250% growth -&gt; 500 million. <b>Correct result, </b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">improbable starting population.</span><br /> 6.7 billion -&gt; 97% dead -&gt; 200 million survive -&gt; 250% growth -&gt; 500 million. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Correct result, </b>maybe plausible numbers.</span><br /> <br /> <u>So out of those I think the numbers were most likely:</u><br /> 5-7 billion -&gt; 95-97% dead -&gt; 200-250 million survivors -&gt; 200-250% growth<br /> <br /> EDIT: 4 billion -&gt; 90-95% dead -&gt; 200-400 million survivors -&gt; 125-250% growth is plausible IMO only if the late First Age did not have 10 billion people","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-17-2015, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T21:45:42-08:00","id":783240,"title":"","content":"Other possiblities: Fiat via plot and what works for what is needed for the Contagion as a narrative element and what is needed for Creation as a setting location. What numbers are there at any time are to support what works for thematics, not to create tidy number-generation.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T22:01:32-08:00","id":783246,"title":"","content":"For me the handwavium type of suspension of disbelief doesn't work. I crave internal consistency in fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T03:16:41-08:00","id":783338,"title":"","content":"Another thing to think about could be that Creation was much bigger before the Contagion and Balorian Crusade. If the majority of the population that died was in the areas that were lost then the death toll numbers, even with Shogunate losses between, start to look reasonable. As well as higher starting populations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T03:24:50-08:00","id":783340,"title":"","content":"The Great Contagion, as an event, should really include the Fair Folk invasion, and all other ancillary deaths. I think the point at which it goes &quot;90% of everything died... and then a whole bunch of other things died the next day&quot;, you're gilding the lily. The deaths that happen as a knock-on effect of those caused by the magical plague should be incorporated into the 90%.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T06:04:20-08:00","id":783404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=783246#post783246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the handwavium type of suspension of disbelief doesn't work. I crave internal consistency in fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the need for consistency over completeness of a setting, while indeed a taste choice, is not a mandatory thing for most settings. Lots of fictioin collapses if you push it too hard and I have found settings which do overdo it with trying ot make everything neatly coherent tend to feel sterile or if anything wasted a lot of wordcount on things that are better left just taken for granted.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like math. Math is never going to be logically complete and consistent. So we generally grant the fiction that it is and still do logical proofs in it as if it were.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T12:08:44-08:00","id":788254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/781307-how-many-dragonblooded-per?p=783340#post783340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Contagion, as an event, should really include the Fair Folk invasion, and all other ancillary deaths. I think the point at which it goes &quot;90% of everything died... and then a whole bunch of other things died the next day&quot;, you're gilding the lily. The deaths that happen as a knock-on effect of those caused by the magical plague should be incorporated into the 90%.</div> </div> </div> </div>I basically agree with you, whether or not the books do. I think 90% is already ridiculous as a setting statement. But if &quot;only&quot; 90% died then either: the human population has not grown at all during the Age of Sorrows, it has continued to fall during the Age of sorrows, it was never 10 billion in the First Age, or about three quarters of humanity died during the Usurpation and Shoguante era.<br /> <br /> I'm comfortable with the First Age having less than 10 billion humans, but I like the idea that it did have a population like ours today, around 6-7 billion. That could make your take plausible without the Usurpation+Shogunate killing over half of humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> But having an advanced civilization requires a certain minimum population, to have enough people with specialized techncial (or magical) knowledge. If you don't also have a lot of automation, you also need enough farmers and laborers/slaves to feed and house everybody. Is the Shogunate really plausible with a total human population of only 2-3 billion? I don't know enough about that era, but my gut feeling is that less than 4 billion is too low.<br /> <br /> <b>So my question is</b>: given what is written about the Shogunate, and <i>ignoring</i> the Contagion, what is a reasonable approximate human population during the Shogunate era? What would make sense with the (few) descriptions of that period, the society and technology, etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-17-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}